@startuml 06_seq_invite_accept
title Tenant onboarding by invitation — admin invite → invitee accepts (ADR-0035)

skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Admin
actor Invitee
participant "MembersController" as MCtrl
participant "InviteService" as Invites
participant "Mailer" as Mail
participant "AuthController" as ACtrl
participant "AuthService" as Auth
participant "UserRepository" as Users

== Invite (admin, inside a tenant) ==
Admin -> MCtrl : POST /members/invites { email }
activate MCtrl
MCtrl -> Invites : invite(email, tenantId, invitedBy)
activate Invites
Invites -> Invites : mint one-time invite token\n(bound to tenant + email)
Invites -> Mail : send invite link (?invite_token=…)
Invites --> MCtrl : { invite }
deactivate Invites
MCtrl --> Admin : 201
deactivate MCtrl
Mail -> Invitee : email with accept link

== Accept (invitee, sets password) ==
Invitee -> ACtrl : POST /auth/accept-invite\n{ invite_token, password }
activate ACtrl
ACtrl -> Auth : acceptInvite(token, password)
activate Auth
Auth -> Invites : consume(token)
Invites --> Auth : { email, tenantId } | invalid
alt token valid & unused
  Auth -> Users : create user in tenantId\n(scrypt hash)
  Auth --> ACtrl : session token
  ACtrl --> Invitee : 204 + Set-Cookie → lands in that tenant
else invalid / expired / used
  Auth --> ACtrl : error
  ACtrl --> Invitee : 400/401 problem+json
end
deactivate Auth
deactivate ACtrl
note over Users : plain /register is left untouched,\nso fresh installs stay single-tenant

@enduml
